    "media:imagetext": "S\nSYDNEY\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nAUSTRALIA can provide the visitor with a range of experiences from attending cultural events in the\nSydney Opera House, pictured here, to visiting aboriginal tribes in the Outback. This continent, as\nlarge as the United States, encompasses many aspects; The Great Barrier Reef, marvelous skiing in\nJuly just 200 miles south of Sydney; bountiful gems and strange animals and birds. Unique flora and\nfauna are here in marvelous abundance. Pan Am serves Sydney and Melbourne from Los Angeles,\nSan Francisco, New York, London, Auckland, Honolulu, and Nadi.\nPAN AM.\n2001. 080.250",
